sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CSS depth, the stereo window rule (ORDER 414d): a popped element whose
    drawn copy, in either eye, reaches a side of the page's viewport that
    lies on the output's edge is drawn at the screen, as the desktop keeps
    anything popped that touches the output's edge at the screen (something in
    front of the screen cut by the screen's edge looks wrong; behind it is
    like looking through a window). The side counts when Stereo KWin lists
    it among the window's edges on the output's edge (kde_stereo_depth_v1,
    output_edges) and the viewport is flush with the window there (a page in
    full screen). Inset elements, sunk elements and a window away from the
    output's edge keep their level; the click area and the scroll frames follow.
  * Every popup is an xdg_popup of its own surface under Stereo KWin: the
    <select> list, tooltips, form autocomplete and the permission prompts were
    wl_subsurfaces of the window, which sit at the window's level, while the
    context menu, an xdg_popup, was popped by the desktop. Now all of them are
    popped, at the same level as a Qt menu on the same output.
    widget.wayland.popups-as-xdg-popups (default true) turns it off for
    Gecko's own choice.
  * about:support tells the truth about DMABuf WebGL on NVIDIA: where an
    output shows stereo 3D the feature is forced on by
    widget.dmabuf-webgl.stereo-nvidia.enabled (the block of Mozilla's bug
    1924578 stays in the decision log), and with that preference false it is
    blocked and says so.
  * The source states what it is: browser commit 9e5eab05c5 (Sparky-OS/waterfox,
    branch stereo3d) in SOURCE.edition.json, debian/browser-build.env and the
    vendor baseline.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

